    "id": "rate_half_ca_hankel_a1_first_degree_core_one_quadratic_gap_four_paired_split_biform_scalar_weld_gate",
    "title": "A=1 quadratic paired split-biform scalar-weld gate",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "joint row and parameter realizability is one augmented full-support kernel condition",
    "statement": "Evaluate the fixed-domain and zero-excess parameter factorizations on their common grid. On every nonincidence cell their nonzero row and fiber scalars must weld. Eliminating the fiber scalars gives a sparse two-entry linear matrix W. The two factorization directions come from one biform if and only if the fixed-domain coefficient-MDS matrix augmented by W has a kernel vector with every coordinate nonzero. In that event the parameter coefficient-MDS gate follows automatically.",
